The 5D SU(2) runs show a clear cold/hot hysteresis gap at beta = 1.6. It is weak and marginal at 1.7, and absent at 1.3, 1.5, 1.9 and 2.2. These are short runs: 200 sweeps of checkerboard Metropolis, one seed per start. They show the gap but don't locate or characterise the transition.

**Control:** the expectation of (1/2)Tr U at beta = 1 is I2(1)/I1(1) = **0.240194**. It is in `control.txt`, and a series and a numerical integral agree. My first `control.py` run crashed because this numpy has no `np.trapz`. That was a defect in my code, and I fixed it and reran.

P is the mean of the last 100 sweeps; the error comes from 10 blocks and ignores autocorrelation.

